btc-verified (Bitcoin CompactSize and related Lean proofs)
==========================================================

Canonical git repository:
	https://github.com/cryptoquick/btc-verified.git

Local path:
	ref/btc-verified (git submodule)

This metadata file:
	ref/btc-verified.SOURCE (sibling of the submodule directory; not inside it)

Pin recorded in this tree:
	Tag:    none (this tree has no release tag at the pin)
	Commit: 6c279c18914f5a22fb33e772f466b9362d6a4fcb

Why this pin:
	Surmount Systems Tech Tree (0011) cites Bitcoin canonical CompactSize as
	proved in Lean in this tree (namespace BtcVerified.CompactSize, theorems
	decode_encode, decode_canonical, and encode_length_le). The publisher
	repository has no release tag at this pin. The submodule is recorded at
	the commit that git submodule add checked out from that URL (master
	HEAD at add time). Surmount specs cite that commit, not a floating
	branch name.

Form:
	Form 1 git submodule from the git URL the operator named for this pin.

License:
	The upstream LICENSE file states Apache License, Version 2.0
	(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Surmount does not own
	that tree; this is a pin of the named git. Numbered specification 0009
	in this repository is Unlicense and does not relicense this pin. See
	also ref/README.md and ref/btc-verified/LICENSE.

How to re-check the pin (from repo root; requires git permission when used
by an agent):
	1. git -C ref/btc-verified describe --tags --always
	2. git -C ref/btc-verified rev-parse HEAD

Do not edit files inside this submodule. Cite the commit instead.
Do not place Surmount-only metadata inside the submodule working tree.
Canonical upstream URL remains first-class; the submodule freezes the
reviewed pin for this repository.
